  "A decaying El Niño left the Pacific drained of warm water, and the trade winds strengthened through 2010. Cold water rose in the east and a strong La Niña followed. Watch Niño 3.4 fall below −1 °C by winter, the thermocline rise in the east, and the Southern Oscillation Index turn positive. Dates and strengths are approximate.": "逐漸衰退的聖嬰現象讓太平洋的暖水流失，2010年全年信風增強。東部冷水湧升，隨後出現強烈的反聖嬰現象。請觀察冬季前Niño 3.4降到−1 °C以下、東部斜溫層變淺、南方振盪指數轉為正值。日期和強度均為近似值。",
